		},
		{
			"ID": "20261018163000-tgvsr1a",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261018163000-tgvsr1a",
				"updated": "20261022132341"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Press Esc on the canvas to return to reading and let the document receive wheel input. If a node editor or relationship-line drag is active, Esc first finishes or cancels that operation. Esc also leaves multi-select mode. In full screen, Esc exits full screen."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261018200107-p7ncdxc",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261018200107-p7ncdxc",
				"updated": "20261020181700"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "You can also hold the middle mouse button and drag to pan temporarily without switching to the hand tool; release it to stop. Hold Ctrl (Command on macOS) and drag the canvas with the right mouse button to pan temporarily without changing keyboard focus or activating a reading canvas. Ordinary wheel input then continues scrolling the document. This gesture is unavailable while the view is locked. Ordinary left dragging on blank canvas selects nodes with a box. For left-button panning, enable "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "More"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " - "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Hand Tool"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": ". While enabled, the toolbar shows a button for leaving this mode directly. On a touchscreen, tap the map to activate the canvas. A quick one-finger drag starting on a node or blank canvas pans the view; to move a node, hold it until the outline appears, then drag. Before activation, one-finger swipes still scroll the document. Two-finger zooming and panning, double-tap editing, and the selection, summary and connection modes keep their existing interactions."
				}
			]
		},
